                                        "entry_id": "6f2cf516-507d-33dc-9fee-30e7003f6b8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A course, or set of courses, that includes (specifically) trigonometry and algebra at an appropriate level to prepare students to study calculus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12a1ee9c-c404-4ac5-9afa-bb782d57896b",
                                                "sense_id": "fe14399a-7482-39dc-81f5-8f0841e9f537",
                                                "text": "2016, Pam Goodner (lead writer/editor), Eureka Math Precalculus Study Guide, Wiley (Jossey-Bass), page ix,\nAs we wrote the Precalculus course, we wanted to create interest for older high school students by presenting topics in a context, something that students could relate to so that they could see the value in their work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd0af53d-d427-43d5-b06f-9f2938726669",
                                                "sense_id": "fe14399a-7482-39dc-81f5-8f0841e9f537",
                                                "text": "2017, Sheldon Axler, Precalculus: A Prelude to Calculus, Wiley, 3rd Edition, page xviii,\nSimilarly, many precalculus textbooks consider, for example, a colony of bacteria doubling in size every 3 hours, with the textbook then producing the formula e/3) for the growth factor after t hours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09284369-dcde-40b4-9b61-673a15ab919c",
                                                "sense_id": "fe14399a-7482-39dc-81f5-8f0841e9f537",
                                                "text": "2023, Mehdi Rahmani-Andebili, Precalculus, Springer, page v,\nMoreover, in many universities and colleges, a precalculus course is mandatory for under-prepared students as the prerequisite course of Calculus 1."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
